## Std\Task — descriptor-owned structured task spawning.
##
## `spawn action` submits a zero-argument closure to the runtime worker pool.
## The compiler supplies a hidden ownership descriptor for the inferred result
## type. Heap results stay alive until their transparent await transfers them
## to the caller; grouped tasks retain an observed result independently of
## group cleanup. Exceptions and cancellation complete without fabricating a
## payload. Submission and completion are thread-safe.
module Std\Task

export spawn

## Run `action` concurrently and transparently await its result at first use.
## Submission failure raises through the normal native-promise call path.
extern native spawn : (() -> result) -> result = "YonaStdTaskSpawn"
